TEXT -128 -168 Left 3 ;#303 Pulse counting FM discriminator (Alan's two-transistor bench circuit)
TEXT -128 -112 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jQlN2fc7LJc
TEXT -128 -72 Left 2 ;Q1 squares up the 100 kHz FM IF; on each falling Q1 edge, CT pulls Q2's emitter below ground and Q2 dumps a fixed charge into RC2,
TEXT -128 -40 Left 2 ;making a narrow negative pulse at PULSE. RLP-CLP averages the pulses, so AUDIO falls as the IF frequency rises.
TEXT -128 488 Left 2 ;VIF stands in for the mixer IF output: 100 kHz, +/-50 kHz deviation, 160 mV p-p (Alan's scope); 500 Hz tone (modulation index 100).
TEXT -128 520 Left 2 ;Assumed (not stated in the video): VCC = 5 V; CLP = 10 nF in place of the stray capacitance and audio-amp bandwidth Alan relies on.
TEXT -128 576 Left 2 !.tran 0 5m 0 20n
TEXT -128 616 Left 2 !.meas tran AUDIO_MAX MAX V(audio) FROM=2m TO=4m
TEXT -128 648 Left 2 !.meas tran AUDIO_MIN MIN V(audio) FROM=2m TO=4m
TEXT -128 680 Left 2 !.meas tran AUDIO_PP PARAM AUDIO_MAX-AUDIO_MIN
TEXT 560 616 Left 2 !.meas tran PW_50K TRIG V(pulse)=2.5 FALL=1 TD=2.99m TARG V(pulse)=2.5 RISE=1 TD=2.99m
TEXT 560 648 Left 2 !.meas tran PW_150K TRIG V(pulse)=2.5 FALL=1 TD=3.99m TARG V(pulse)=2.5 RISE=1 TD=3.99m
TEXT 560 680 Left 2 !.meas tran AVG_150K AVG V(pulse) FROM=3.95m TO=4.05m
TEXT 560 712 Left 2 !.meas tran AVG_50K AVG V(pulse) FROM=2.95m TO=3.05m
